  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "PeerSharp 5.1.0 makes streaming to other devices work well: HttpStreamServer is socket-based and can serve a TV or cast receiver on the network, with an access token, CORS and files served beside the stream; Settings.Streaming tunes read-ahead and waits; a stream's pieces are fetched first, from every peer and web seed that has them, and spread across the swarm. It fixes uTP connections that stopped receiving, and hardens handshakes and encryption, piece verification, peer and DHT input, proxies, NAT mappings, bandwidth limiting, resume data and engine lifecycles. Passing a bare null as HttpStreamServer's third constructor argument is now ambiguous. See https://github.com/ligenq/PeerSharp/blob/v5.1.0/CHANGELOG.md.",
